    description: "This is the mid-range machine that measures best where it counts. Its 60-inch belt yielded 58.5 inches of genuinely usable deck, which was the best result outside the commercial machines and a full inch better than one competitor quoting the same belt figure. Combined with the 22-inch width, our 6'5\" tester recorded fewer than one rail strike per 45-minute run, against four on the 20-inch decks. None of the three testers reported shortening their stride at 9 mph, which is the subjective measure that tracks everything else. The frame is heavy enough to stay entirely still through 10 mph blocks. The screen tilts, which sounds trivial and solves a real irritation for anyone looking down at a fixed console. The subscription orientation of the software is the only meaningful complaint, and it does not touch the hardware.",
  },
