  },
  {
    id: "proform-pro-2000",
    name: "ProForm Pro 2000",
    category: "Best Budget 60-Inch Deck",
    badge: "Best Budget",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/s?k=ProForm%20Pro%202000+Treadmill&tag=sktiger-20",
    reviewUrl: "/proform-pro-2000-treadmill/",
    priceRange: "$899-$1,199",
    specs: "60 in. belt / 57.5 in. usable · 20 in. wide · 3.0 CHP · -3% to 12%",
    pros: [
      "A genuine 60-inch belt for around a thousand dollars",
      "Folds, which nothing else on this list does",
      "Decline included at a price where it is normally absent",
      "Adequate for a lighter tall runner at moderate paces",
    ],
    cons: [
      "Lowest usable length here at 57.5 inches — the belt figure flatters it",
      "Frame moves perceptibly at 9 mph and above",
    ],
    bottomLine: "The cheapest route to a 60-inch belt, with the smallest usable deck behind that figure. Best for lighter tall runners at moderate pace.",
    description: "The Pro 2000 is here because it answers a real question: what is the least you can spend and still get a 60-inch belt? At around a thousand dollars, this is it, and for a tall runner on a firm budget that is worth knowing. Two honest caveats follow. First, the usable-length measurement was the lowest in the test at 57.5 inches — the advertised 60 is a belt figure and this machine loses more of it to the rear roller than the others do, so it is meaningfully shorter in practice than the spec sheet implies. Second, the frame moves at 9 mph and above, which our heavier testers noticed on longer efforts. It also folds, which no other machine here does and which matters if the room has another use. For a lighter tall runner doing steady mileage rather than hard intervals, it is a defensible buy.",
  },
];

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      itemListElement: [
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "Best Lists", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/best-of/" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 3, name: "Best Treadmills for Tall Runners", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/best-treadmills-for-tall-runners/" },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      mainEntity: [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "What size treadmill deck do I need if I am over 6 feet?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Sixty inches of belt is the minimum and we would not recommend anything shorter at any price. Above 6'4\", also look for a 22-inch width rather than 20, because a longer stride comes with wider natural foot placement and our tallest tester recorded four rail strikes per run on 20-inch belts against fewer than one on 22-inch ones.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Is advertised belt length the same as usable deck length?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "No, and the gap varies by brand. Belt length includes the section wrapping down onto the rear roller, which is not somewhere you want to land. Usable length ran one to two inches shorter across the machines we measured, and two treadmills quoting the same 60-inch belt differed by a full inch of usable deck.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "What ceiling height do I need for a treadmill?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Take your height, add the deck height (6 to 10 inches), add roughly 4 inches for incline at higher grades, then add 3 to 4 inches of stride bounce. A 6'3\" runner on an 8-inch deck at 10% incline needs comfortably over 7 feet 6 inches. Standard 8-foot ceilings work; basements with ducting and sloped loft ceilings frequently do not.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Why does treadmill running feel unnatural when you are tall?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Almost always because the deck is too short and you are subconsciously shortening your stride to stay clear of the rear roller. That produces a choppier gait with more calf work and less hip extension than your outdoor running, which is also why treadmill-specific calf and Achilles complaints are common. A 60-inch deck largely resolves it.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Do I need a treadmill that reaches 12 mph?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Rarely. Twelve mph is a 5-minute mile, and most machines that display it become unpleasant to run on well below it. What matters far more is whether the frame is stable and quiet at 9 to 10 mph, where hard sessions actually happen. Judge on stability at realistic paces, not on the top number the console will show.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Is a wider belt worth paying for?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Above about 6'4\", yes. Twenty inches is standard and adequate for most runners; 22 inches gives margin for the wider foot placement that comes with a longer stride and for the way placement wanders as you fatigue. Below 6'3\" most runners will not notice the difference on runs under an hour.",
          },
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      headline: title,
      description: description,
      author: { "@type": "Person", name: "Morgan Reyes" },
      datePublished: "2026-09-08",
      dateModified: "2026-09-08",
      publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Treadmill Reviews USA" },
    },
    ...PRODUCTS.map((product) => ({
      "@type": "Product",
      name: product.name,
      description: product.description,
      brand: { "@type": "Brand", name: product.name.split(" ")[0] },
      offers: {
        "@type": "AggregateOffer",
        priceCurrency: "USD",
        availability: "https://schema.org/InStock",
      },
    })),
  ],
};
---

